    "result_text": "The build is green. The full `mvn test` compiles everything (regenerating `OwnerDto` from the openapi spec and the MapStruct mapper) and runs the suite successfully.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented `membershipNumber` (formatted `<customerCode>-M<YY>`) with minimal structural impact by adding a small, cohesive unit rather than growing any existing class:\n\n1. **`OwnerMembershipPolicy.java`** (new, self-contained) \u2014 a single static `membershipNumber(Owner)` that derives `<customerCode>-M<YY>` from the owner's own `customerCode` and `registrationDate` (YY = `year % 100`), returning `null` if either is absent. This mirrors the existing `Owner*Policy` pattern.\n\n2. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a read-only `membershipNumber` property to the `Owner` schema, which regenerates `OwnerDto` with the getter/setter.\n\n3. **`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added one `@Mapping(... expression ...)` line to `toOwnerDto`, exactly like the existing `displayName` mapping.\n\nBecause the value is derived at read time from the owner's own persisted fields, it's automatically consistent and seed-independent, and required no changes to the `Owner` entity, controller, or service. The acceptance test `coreMembershipNumberFormat` and the full suite pass.",
